From: BE-IIS <info@be-iis.eu>
Subject: [PATCH] media: imx708: increase GMSL2 line lengths

Increase LINE_LENGTH_PCK for both non-HDR modes used through the
MAX96717/MAX96716A GMSL2 path:

- 4608x2592 full resolution: 0x3d20 -> 0x4000
- 2304x1296 2x2 binned:     0x1e90 -> 0x2000

The full-resolution value remains exactly twice the binned value. The
additional horizontal blanking provides more inter-line spacing for the
serializer, deserializer and Raspberry Pi CFE path. Keep the mode
descriptions synchronized with the sensor register lists so that the
V4L2 HBLANK control reports the correct values.

--- a/imx708.c
+++ b/imx708.c
@@ -297,2 +297,2 @@ static const struct imx708_reg mode_4608x2592_regs[] = {
-	{0x0342, 0x3D},
-	{0x0343, 0x20},
+	{0x0342, 0x40},
+	{0x0343, 0x00},
@@ -390,2 +390,2 @@ static const struct imx708_reg mode_2x2binned_regs[] = {
-	{0x0342, 0x1E},
-	{0x0343, 0x90},
+	{0x0342, 0x20},
+	{0x0343, 0x00},
@@ -681 +681 @@ static const struct imx708_mode supported_modes_10bit_no_hdr[] = {
-		.line_length_pix = 0x3d20,
+		.line_length_pix = 0x4000,
@@ -702 +702 @@ static const struct imx708_mode supported_modes_10bit_no_hdr[] = {
-		.line_length_pix = 0x1e90,
+		.line_length_pix = 0x2000,
